{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1488093-recruiting-mummy-the-curse-2nd-edition","id":1488093,"title":"[Recruiting]Mummy: The Curse 2nd Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play","Play by Post"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-26T14:48:02-07:00","id":1488093,"title":"[Recruiting]Mummy: The Curse 2nd Edition","content":"I need three players, with myself as GM. You\u2019d be members of a meret, of the five Guilds out of the corebook. We\u2019d play around with asynchronous time, weaving together a tale of a self-fulfilling prophecy. The PCs must thwart the prophecy, only to find out it was THEY would set the whole thing in motion to deal with an even bigger threat. Big cosmic mysteries and body horror would be the theme of the campaign, a sort of gnostic quest filled with extremely the horrors of Duat liberally peppered throughout.<br /> <br /> The game would stay as Mummy-focused as possible. The other splats certainly exist as written, but I\u2019m wanting to focus on the Mummy side of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T13:19:17-07:00","id":1488201,"title":"","content":"We do not have to limit ourselves to familiar parts of the world. Any area in any country on any continent is a viable choice. It just can\u2019t be Antarctica.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, if you see a setting writeup for another gameline you liked, we can always explore the Arisen side of that area.<br /> <br /> EDIT: To be honest, I\u2019d like somewhere in Eastern Europe or maybe India. Hinduism would accept mummy cults as \u2018just more gods\u2019 and nobody would bat an eye at what in the West would be considered wildly strange. The River Ganges would feature prominently in the flow of Sekhem, a strange supernatural purity somehow parallel the river\u2019s deeply polluted waters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 07-27-2022, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T02:50:46-07:00","id":1488248,"title":"","content":"MtC in India would be very interesting to me. If we want to explore things of body horror, I'd strongly recommend the temple of Kamakhya, in Assam (North of India). The area is strongly associated with strange traditions differing strongly from the rest of India - for example, the temple is not far from Mayong, sometimes dubbed the &quot;capital of black magic&quot; in India. The temple itself is the stage for annual rituals where performers, the Deodhani, cover their skin in the red cinnabar of the Brahmaputra river that flows nearby (this dye is seen as the blood of either Kamakhya, the Goddess worshipped at the temple, or Sati) and start dancing until they get possessed by one of the deities worshipped in the temple - like Manasa, the local snake-goddess and mistress of venoms, or Smaashanakali, Kali of the Funerary Ashes, or Chhinamasta, who holds forth her own decapitated head to drink the blood from her own severed neck... so yeah, pretty Mummy-fitting all in all.<br /> <br /> Of course, we can pick anything else, but since I have to study this specific area for my uni, contributing to a setting doc would be a great way to combine fun and work for me lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T09:01:48-07:00","id":1488262,"title":"","content":"Excellent! Any idea what you\u2019d play?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T16:41:32-07:00","id":1488407,"title":"","content":"Not sure yet: a random concept that popped in my head was a Lion (or Jackal) Sesha-Hebsu that used to secretly love a member of the Dancing Guild of Kehetkhat... only to get sincerely rattled by the Deceiver betrayal. She's now morbidly obsessed with neutralizing future threats, even when the prophecies she hears are obviously biased, vague, or fabricated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T10:53:34-07:00","id":1488470,"title":"","content":"Hmmm. A Deceived archnemesis! Interesting.<br /> <br /> As to the setting idea you prompted. I really like it. The bizarre to Western sensibilities religious clime of the area would allow the Arisen to be a lot more open with Affinities and Utterances and relics. Plus, Hindu folklore is full of enchanted objects I can stat up as relics. As with any Mummy: The Curse game, finding relics and vestiges will be a top priority!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T18:15:28-07:00","id":1488516,"title":"","content":"Plus, the Bagavad Gita has some crazy imagery in it, it\u2019s too good NOT to use!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T09:43:25-07:00","id":1488573,"title":"","content":"Anybody else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T12:01:35-07:00","id":1488591,"title":"","content":"Ok, some preliminary setting information:<br /> <br /> Mummies have been in India a <i>very</i> long time, and the entire country seems awash in relics, Vestiges and Sekhem. Kamakhya is ground zero for several feuding Arisen cults, who use the overwhelming presence of belief in magic and the supernatural to openly perform Utterances.<br /> <br /> <i>Unfortunately</i>...hungry ravenous ghosts of things that never lived, the div, have plagued the temple complex since time immemorial. The div were never human, but exactly <i>what</i> they are is unclear. The div have a hunger for Sekhem, though, and viciously feud with local Arisen over vessels of all sorts. The div are statted up as Rank 2 and Rank 3 ghosts, but rumors of particularly large and bloated \u2018elders\u2019 have persisted down the millennia.<br /> <br /> Because cults feud so viciously over Kamakhya and it\u2019s pilgrims and priests, the Guilds in the region are deeply divided. It\u2019s not to the point of open sectarian conflict, but it <i>could</i>, in theory, get there. The Tef-Aabhi currently hold the upper hand, as their cults designed many of the country\u2019s grandest temples.<br /> <br /> EDIT: All the splats are obviously in India, but the few times they cross paths with the Arisen it is usually blood and Utterance vs fang and Gift, as the wolf children of Wepwawet hold secret rites in Kamakhya that mummies are never allowed to attend. The Arisen, not wanting conflict, simply do as the wolfmen ask.<br /> <br /> The Ganges River is a natural channel for Sekhem, an odd spiritual purity for such a mundanely polluted river. Arisen find that they can briefly lengthen their Descents by bathing in the Ganges, though not by more than a few days. Furthermore, there are rumors\u2014-never substantiated!\u2014-that Su-Menent have figured out a way to store Pillars <i>in</i> the river, as opposed to a cultist or a lesser immortal.<br /> <br /> EDIT2: Considering the blood motif Kamakhya\u2019s celebrations revere, among the lesser Immortals, in this area blood bathers would be most common. Most are grim-faced bearded Brahmin, practicing Rites so old even <i>they</i> can\u2019t ascertain a beginning. They honor obscure, strange gods and are deliberately severe in personality. They have a taciturn relationship with the Arisen, a grudging respect that nevertheless has a profound echo of envy.<br /> <br /> EDIT3: The Red Priest, a Deceived, is the bogeyman of Kamakhya. Whether he even exists in unclear. But the div call him their brother, and practice strange rituals in his name. No one has seen the Red Priest, and evidence for his very existence is, at best, circumstantial.<br /> <br /> EDIT4: Known only to the Arisen, there\u2019re cave entrances protected by powerful Utterances that lead to deep within the earth beneath Kamakhya. At the very bottom is a cave barely large enough for a Size 5 creature to fit into...and a <i>crack</i> in the wall, leading...<i>somewhere</i>. Kepher detects something of great value in Sekhem on the other side, but none can get to it, quite yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 08-01-2022, 06:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T16:19:30-07:00","id":1488745,"title":"","content":"<b>The Deceived</b><br /> The Deceived do not exist. They died during the Rite of Return. Any stories to the contrary are heresy.<br /> <br /> ...so, <i>of course</i> a Deceived dwells here. The Red Priest, a horrifying aberration of a bloated, <i>vastly</i> obese man, sits crippled on his throne, gestating Amkhata in a womb he made inside himself with knives and clamps and industrial-scale paperclips. Flies gather to him, and beetles root through his viscera. He is a mad monster, and his cultists are quite zealous in preserving his secrets, no matter the cost. He rants and he raves, but often sits drooling for weeks on end.<br /> <br /> The Red Priest has an alliance with the daitya, though no one can be sure of that. Circumstantial evidence certainly <i>points</i> to it.<br /> <br /> <b>The Shuankhsen</b><br /> Though she is worshipped under the name Kali, Shuankhsen recognize their hateful mother anywhere they go, no matter the name mortals apply to her. The Thuggee were a series of Shuankhsen cults.<br /> <br /> <b>The Kher-Minu</b><br /> A single Kher-Minu, an unknown male, guards Kamakhya as a whole. He says nothing, just obeying mutely any commands a Deathless gives him. It has been three centuries since his last activation.<br /> <br /> <b>Maar-Kherit</b><br /> Kamakhya\u2019s Su-Menent have a secret. Hidden away, somewhere in the temple complex, is a library containing knowledge of Maar-Kherit activities in India. The Priests guard this lore zealously.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, no Maar-Kherit are in or near Kamakhya.<br /> <br /> <b>The Daitya of Kamakhya</b><br /> Though the Deathless have many theories, none can satisfactorily explain the daitya. Ghosts from some prehuman civilizations, these Pygmy-sized insectile spectres hunger for Sekhem as badly as do the Deceived and the Shuankhsen. Resembling one meter tall, rain thin humanoids of an indeterminate insect species, the daitya speak in buzzing voices and rant of a coming time when humanity is as dust on the wind, and of consciousnesses echoed down millions of years to \u201cprepare the way\u201d.<br /> <br /> They cannot use Manifestations during the day, but are otherwise unaffected by sunlight. Certain Hindu prayers drive them away, but also, certain antediluvian Rites can call them forth. They nest in great spirit-burrows in Neter-Khertet, fighting a never-ending war with Duat\u2019s fiends.<br /> <br /> Most daitya are statted up as Rank 2 or Rank 3 ghosts, with Anchors of unknown origin. (At least, they\u2019ve yet to be found.) Rumors speak of much larger daitya at Rank 4 or even Rank 5, though no Memories record such an encounter.<br /> <br /> The daitya are found only in Kamakhya, nowhere else. Their burrows do not match any locality in the physical world, but are <i>clearly</i> nonetheless in Nether-Khertet. They call the Red Priest a brother in their practices.<br /> <br /> The language they speak among themselves in unintelligible, but many know various Indian languages. They claim to have been once much different than they are now, and bitterly anticipate the coming of a far-distant enemy.<br /> <br /> <b>Other supernatural entities of Kamakhya</b><br /> <b>Beasts</b><br /> The Begotten sometimes pay the temple complex a visit. It always heralds, as the Chinese say, \u201cinteresting times\u201d.<br /> <br /> <b>Changelings</b><br /> Hmmm. Pondering ideas, now.<br /> <br /> <b>Demons</b><br /> Kamakhya is <i>old</i> Infrastructure and, though the Arisen know it not, the temple complex is protected by a powerful angel.<br /> <br /> <b>Deviants</b><br /> \u201cThe what, now?\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>Leviathans</b><br /> The Wicked Tribe covets Kamakhya. The Arisen refuse to relinquish it. Trouble is eventually <i>guaranteed</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Mages</b><br /> In the 1890s, British Mages feuded with the Arisen for control over Kamakhya. They lost; the Arisen won. The Awakened are <i>much</i> more circumspect in their dealings with the Deathless, now.<br /> <br /> They <i>are</i> curious of the daitya but refuse to say why.<br /> <br /> <b>Prometheans</b><br /> Strange things happen, sometimes, such as the False Azar. He claimed he was of Azar\u2019s blood, though Kamakhya\u2019s mummies sensed the wrongness in him. They drove him out with fire and Utterances, and he\u2019s never been seen since.<br /> <br /> <b>Sin-Eaters</b><br /> Some mortals come close to the Arisen in necromantic might, though the Deathless are unclear as to the specifics. They are cordial to visiting Sin-Eaters, and promptly usher them on their after a few pleasantries. They keep <i>coming back</i>, however, and\u2019re mightily interested in the daitya.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampires</b><br /> They come here to feed during festivals, and are vaguely aware of the Deathless. They call themselves \u201cthe Crone\u2019s circle\u201d and practice magic as unnatural as any Utterance. They respect the \u201cenlightened vampires\u201d (ie, the Arisen), and don\u2019t cause much trouble.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolves</b><br /> India\u2019s werewolves claim an ancient right to the territory of Kamakhya, but cannot dislodged the Arisen and have since ceased trying. (Some sort of wolfman-only sectarian conflict has demanded their attention for centuries now. They refuse to elaborate.)<br /> <br /> On certain days of the years, the werewolves politely ask for sole possession of the temple-complex for the next twenty four hours. The Deathless oblige, though beforehand they set wards and Sadikhs to keep watch tombs and relics, and afterwards they always paranoiacly check for lingering magics. Eventually, this compromise will fall through, but it\u2019s workable for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 11-10-2022, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T00:30:25-07:00","id":1488769,"title":"","content":"Very nice ! To limit my nerd info-bombing, I'm starting a google doc with interesting informations related to Kamakhya, Assam and ChroD implementation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15CfcTZxedhjkS29zx58gXvnOX129I7MrHB_pHr4NrRA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15CfcTZxedhjkS29zx58gXvnOX129I7MrHB_pHr4NrRA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15CfcTZxedhjkS29zx58gXvnOX129I7MrHB_pHr4NrRA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/15CfcTZxedhjkS29zx58gXvnOX129I7MrHB_pHr4NrRA/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T06:08:30-07:00","id":1488811,"title":"","content":"Modified a few things...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T18:42:46-07:00","id":1488912,"title":"","content":"<b>The Maa-Kep</b><br /> Not sure, yet, still pondering.<br /> <br /> <b>The Mesen-Nebu</b><br /> Money flows into holy places like a flowing river, constant and steady, and the Mesen-Nebu are there to reap it all. Civil servants and outside contractors are hired on a weekly basis. In this way, the Born of Gold have their fingers in the Kamakhya pie.<br /> <br /> <b>The Sesha-Hebsu</b><br /> Many Brahmins serve in Sesha-Hebsu cults, finding that Guild\u2019s obsession with the Scroll of Ages to be fascinating.<br /> <br /> More than that, the Sesha-Hebsu are in Kamakhya looking into the idea of the Mahashruti, or \u201cauthorless books\u201d, which they believe is simply the Hindu name for the Scroll of Ages, or else a mortal reflection of it. Studying and comparing these two concepts of knowledge take up a lot of Sesha-Hebsu cultists\u2019 time.<br /> <br /> <b>The Su-Menent</b><br /> Surprisingly, the Su-Menent are rather weakly represented in Kamakhya. There are only two of them. Their cults, however, are huge, highly literate and keep several repositories of occult knowledges.<br /> <br /> <b>The Tef-Aabhi</b><br /> The Tef-Aabhi reign supreme in Kamakhya, which is, interestingly enough, mostly Neithian architecture. Dedwen flows pure and hale here, and using Kepher is much easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 08-03-2022, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T20:59:39-07:00","id":1488930,"title":"","content":"Tef-Aabhi reigning on Kamakhya makes sense, the sculptures there are superb, and only the Architects have the influence over populations needed to keep a temple relevant from the 7th century up to this day. Interestingly enough, the most important and sacred item in the temple is not a human representation: it's a pierced stone kept inside the most sacred and remote room of the temple, representing the <i>yoni</i> (womb) of the Goddess in her form of Sati, fallen there after she jumped in a pyre...<br /> <br /> Also, common misconception, but...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1488093-recruiting-mummy-the-curse-2nd-edition?p=1488912#post1488912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> More than that, the Sesha-Hebsu are in Kamakhya looking into the idea of the Akashic Record, which they believe is simply the Hindu name for the Scroll of Ages. That mere mortals claim to\u2019ve accessed it both offends and intrigues them, in equal measure.</div> </div> </div> </div>... the Akashic Records are not really a hindu thing: they're a latter concept of Theosophy, an occult Western current that had a great influence in the end of the 19th century. Akasha is one of the elements and associated with sound, but no hindi sources I know describes it as memory storage. In one of the great religious currents, shaivism, <i>trik\u0101laj\u00f1atvam</i>, the knowledge of past and future, is supposed to be one of the siddhis you gain through meditation and spiritual practices - but it's seen as a power of the devotee freeing himself from the illusory world, not tapping a preexisting archive.<br /> <br /> There's a set of notions in Indian philosophy we can levy though. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C5%9Aruti\" target=\"_blank\">Shruti</a> is the corpus of indian sacred texts that are <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apauru%E1%B9%A3ey%C4%81\" target=\"_blank\">apaurusheya</a>, authorless (as opposed to smrti, traceable tradition where you can point the author). The very process of commiting them to memory and being able to restitute them at the drop of a hat, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sv%C4%81dhy%C4%81ya\" target=\"_blank\">sv\u0101dhy\u0101ya</a> (&quot;the Lesson of the Self&quot;, or &quot;Lesson of the Soul&quot;), is deemed a devotional act.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, Sesha-Hebsu in India would probably qualify the Scroll of Ages as Shruti (or maybe with an intensified prefix &gt; Mahashruti, &quot;the Great Tradition&quot;), or Sv\u0101dhy\u0101ya.<br /> <br /> I'll see if I can find something about Maa-kep and amulets !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","user":"Adrasalieth","date":". 08-03-2022, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T14:58:50-07:00","id":1489018,"title":"","content":"Thanks! I\u2019ll make changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T18:10:25-07:00","id":1489039,"title":"","content":"<b>Iremite religion and the faith of Hinduism</b><br /> To be blunt, benevolent gods are not part of the pantheon of Irem. No, to the Nameless Empire, the gods are divine monsters too powerful to interact with directly without going mad. The wine of Shezmu is distilled human suffering.<br /> <br /> Hinduism, while it has gods as cruel as any Judge of Duat, <i>has</i> a great number of <i>very</i> benign divinities. Vishnu has repeatedly set himself to Earth in avatar form to help save the world, the most famous of which is Krishna. Gods, Hindus believe, have and indeed a great many possess similar temperaments.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation, however, is a thorny subject for the Arisen. They have something <i>like</i> reincarnation with their Descents, but close examinations causes the similarities to disintegrate. Shades in Duat either ascend to A\u2019aru or are crushed by Shezmu\u2019s stomping feet, or worse, Fed to Ammut. This is an irrevocable journey.<br /> <br /> As a result, syncretizint \u201cthe true faith\u201d (as the Arisen see it) with Hinduism takes some doing. Certain Hindu deities, however, are <i>very</i> Familiar to mummies. Who is Kali? Who is Shiva? Ammut. Whether this is true or not is a matter of some significant debate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T09:42:03-07:00","id":1489126,"title":"","content":"<b>Sekhem sorcery in Kamakhya</b><br /> In many religions, the division between praying and casting a spell is irrelevant, and Kamakhya is no different. Due its long dominance by the Arisen, the temple complex has a sacred tradition of Sekhem sorcery, in addition to the fell magic titled Blood bathing.<br /> <br /> Several Open Rites are practiced in Kamakhya, but it\u2019s Closed Rites are particularly interesting, as they affect daityas, Amkhata and fiends, most through exorcisms.<br /> <br /> <b>Ghosts in Kamakhya</b><br /> At least one Avernian Gate is in Kamakhya, protected by a geist called the Headless Guru, and several other places exist, Resonant with death but not quite portals to other realms. <br /> <br /> By meditating at these places long enough and with the assistance of three Sekhem casters casting the same Closed Rite, a mummy can enter...<i>another</i> Neter-Khertet. It is no desert, has no storms, is under no Law of Suffering....just lost and lonely and dim. Mummies can never stay in these strange \u201cother-Twilights\u201d for more than a few minutes, and the Judges flay the Deathless\u2019 Sekhem in retribution. In truly awfully cases, Anpu himself will arrive and unceremoniously deposit the Arisen back in the mortal plane.<br /> <br /> <b>Vessels in Kamakhya</b><br /> Several Vessels\u2019ve been gathered over the centuries and not offered up to the Judges for whatever reason.<br /> <b>Kamakhya\u2019s Relics</b><br /> The Gong of Monkeys and Laughter and Tears (Regia **):<br /> A small bronze gong emblazoned with monkey motifs, mostly of monkeys being pranky, this relic appeared out of nowhere in the court of an early emperor of the Qin dynasty.<br /> Stats coming soon.<br /> <br /> Rudyard Kipling\u2019s Thumb (Uter *):<br /> Yes, really.<br /> Stats soon coming.<br /> <br /> Swords of Samsara (Regia *****):<br /> Stats soon coming.<br /> <br /> <b>Kamakhya\u2019s Vestiges</b><br /> The Golden Book (Text ***; a copy of the Bhagavad Gita).<br /> <br /> Idol of Kali (Regia *).<br /> <br /> The Sunken Mandala (Text ***).<br /> A great prayer-wheel kept by Kamakhya\u2019s Arisen, it\u2019s artistry depicts a strange scene: ancient Egyptians fighting what was been determined to be <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea_Peoples\" target=\"_blank\">the Sea People</a>. The writing, however, is in Sanskrit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 11-11-2022, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T09:22:46-07:00","id":1489556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1488093-recruiting-mummy-the-curse-2nd-edition?p=1488573#post1488573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anybody else?</div> </div> </div> </div>In Rome - Italy is really a pyramid in the middle of the city.<br /> The pyramid was built around the 12 B.C. for a famous tribune of those days: Caio Cestio Epulone. Hence its name &quot;Cestia Pyramid&quot;.<br /> In that age, Egypt was a province of Rome and its customs was the fashion of the moment. The rich tribune commissioned a pyramid as his future burial place.<br /> The task had to be fulfilled by his sons within an year from his death or they would have lost the rich inheritance. The pyramid was completed even earlier. Miracle of money god.<br /> <br /> In the Chronicles of Darkness i was thinking as if Cestio uncovered the secrets of the rite of return during a journey in egypt.<br /> He craved for the power to vanquish death, but never fully understood the price he had to pay to the judges.<br /> He returned Rome with the ritual details and commissioned the pyramid. Nobody paid attention to a rich old man eccentricities. Not even his sons, interested only in his riches.<br /> Cestio died soon after under misterious circumstances, and his unaware sons performed the burial ritual as requested by his father.<br /> From that moment on, Caio Cestio became an eternal presence under the soil of the eternal city.<br /> No one ever suspected of ancient horrors from egypt to lurk underground in the middle of Rome.<br /> <br /> Actually the pyramid is a monument that can be visited by everyone, but Caio's burial chamber was never found. It's walled beneath a fake chamber that is believed nowaday to be the original.<br /> There's no better place to hide something than under the nose of everyone.<br /> <br /> The pyramid still stands today in the middle of a <a href=\"https://www.google.it/maps/@41.8765128,12.4813052,3a,75y,265.92h,96.9t/data=!3m7!1e1!3m5!1slGJ-otRnGryda4FoojsdeQ!2e0!6shttps:%2F%2Fstreetviewpixels-pa.googleapis.com%2Fv1%2Fthumbnail%3Fpanoid%3DlGJ-otRnGryda4FoojsdeQ%26cb_client%3Dmaps_sv.tactile.gps%26w%3D203%26h%3D100%26yaw%3D291.72247%26pitch%3D0%26thumbfov%3D100!7i16384!8i8192?hl=it\" target=\"_blank\">heavy trafficed road inside Rome</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26941,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26941-brax79","user":"Brax79","date":". 08-09-2022, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26941-brax79","name":"Brax79","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T09:54:46-07:00","id":1489563,"title":"","content":"No, I\u2019ll have to scuttle the idea of anyone discovering the Rite of Return. And your character has to be Iremitic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T09:12:31-07:00","id":1489642,"title":"","content":"The idea of la Piramide Cestia to be a tomb would be something really cool ! But yeah, personally I feel it makes more sense if the gens Cestii (the family of Gaius Cestius) was a cult devoted to a mummy.<br /> <br /> Gaius Cestius was one of the epulones, a strong political college of priests ruling Roman celebrations - and roman priests were both administrators, ritualists and seers. It makes sense that a mummy would want control of that - and that such an organization would survive through time, with members hidden in the government and the church...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T09:19:22-07:00","id":1489644,"title":"","content":"If you can find a way to link Ancient Rome with a Hindu temple in India....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T14:03:15-07:00","id":1489675,"title":"","content":"<b>Amkhata</b><br /> Several Amkhata are in Kamakhya, imprisoned in Twilight inside statues, prayer wells and ceremonial bells. They cannot escape of their own volition, but the Ted-Aabhi\u2019s primary cult has a different Closed Rite to release each Amkhata.<br /> <br /> <b>peret</b><br /> Not all physically embodied undead are mummies and vampires. The Peret, for instance, is something that never lived, yet retains a strong presence in India. A tiny undead worm, a Peret burrows into the living. The host breaks outin sores, lesions, boils and rashes, making them easy to mistake for leper\u2019s.<br /> <br /> The host is driven, slowly but surely, to commit heinous acts of ever-greater depravity to feed the chaotic whims of the peret inside them.<br /> <br /> From whence did the peret come? Is it of Duat, some sort of permanently embodied fiend? Is something the wolfmen refers to as a doo\u2019gah\u2019theem (whatever <i>that</i> is)? Or has it been hereall along?<br /> <br /> No one knows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 08-11-2022, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T19:19:30-07:00","id":1489704,"title":"","content":"Oh, Andrasalieth, I re-checked the Google doc, and saw you\u2019d updated it! Thanks! It makes my job a frickton easier!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T09:25:53-07:00","id":1489748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1488093-recruiting-mummy-the-curse-2nd-edition?p=1489644#post1489644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you can find a way to link Ancient Rome with a Hindu temple in India....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not that difficult, actually. The Piramide Cestia was built around 16 BCE, under the reign of Augustus (first emperor of Rome after the Republic), which is precisely the time when documented trade started between Rome and South Asian kingdoms: resources traded included incense, spice, pearls and exotic animals. If a mummy is indeed lying there, it might either come directly from India, or having intended to go there.<br /> <br /> Glad you like some of the proposals ! It gives me a fun way to engage with a class subject, lol. I'll try to also provide some background about historical and actual Assam, to complete the &quot;supernatural&quot; folklore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T19:36:57-07:00","id":1489826,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I see your point. It <i>can</i> be done. Brax79? If you\u2019re still interested, the character idea is fine. My only objection is someone knowing the Rite of Return.<br /> <br /> Adrasalieth, feel free to brew up new ideas with your real-world knowledge of Kamakhya!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T03:38:07-07:00","id":1489865,"title":"","content":"Effectively, my interest was in having the tomb in Rome's downtown. If the mummy inhabiting it, is Gaius himself or another mummy that seized control of his tomb is the same for me.<br /> The character personality is a manipulative politician. If it's Gaius or someone else who stole his identity and tomb to assert control in Rome is still fine for me.<br /> I'll provide character's details","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26941-brax79","name":"Brax79","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T09:06:35-07:00","id":1489888,"title":"","content":"....to remind you, this particular game is set in Kamakhya, India. Not Rome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T10:30:19-07:00","id":1489899,"title":"","content":"Weren't we able to start anywhere in the world but Antarctica?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26941-brax79","name":"Brax79","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T11:35:56-07:00","id":1489905,"title":"","content":"I meant the game as a whole. And anyways, I\u2019m not the one you need to convince. I\u2019ll put the game wherever you guys can agree on. Talk to Andrasalieth!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T14:49:20-07:00","id":1491951,"title":"","content":"We still have one slot open! (Assuming Brat79 is still interested.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T16:25:44-07:00","id":1493364,"title":"","content":"I'd also have an interest if there's still room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T16:38:27-07:00","id":1493366,"title":"","content":"Yay! Do you have a character idea, yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T18:08:19-07:00","id":1493373,"title":"","content":"If the game is set in India, I think I may have something. How would you feel about a Kheru priestess and journeyman to the Mesen-Nebu. In her mortal days she was raised in the temples complexes of Bubastis and served as a healer and pourer of the sacred libations to the gods. Her talents drew her to Irem, and in the course of eternity led her to the service of Tutuutef in the afterlife. The tale of the Eye of Ra, and the transformation of the bloodthirsty Sekhmet into the more sedate goddess Bast (among other associations) fell within the pervue of Tutuutef's prohibition of indulging appetites reactively, and his chosen animal was sacred in that part of the Nameless Empire (quick aside, he is surprisingly the only Judge that uses cats as his motiff rather than lions or leopards). In her own existence she has striven for some of this same duality, exploring the world with a calm professional detachment one day while occasionally indulging in a wild hedonism in measured doses. Her cult has migrated from Egypt to Greece (where it adapted into a Mystery Cult based around Dionysius and appropriating more ancient rituals into his bacchannalian rites. She was pushed from that region by Roman conquest and resettled in the heart of India (where her cult has enjoyed modest success by synchronizing itself with certain aspects of the goddess Kali. Her cult is not as prosperous as it once was (the mercurial nature of the Mughals and the British aligned more clearly with the ideals of Dedwen than the current government) but it remains strong. Within the Guilds she is well respected by fellow Mesen-Nebu but are shakier ground with other Arisen. She has a reputation as a Lingerer, for one, pursuing her summoned Purpose with dedication yet spending her remaining time on more frivolous and personal pursuits. She has also embraced stronger than others the philosophies of reincarnation. Unknown to most fellow Arisen, she has tried over the centuries to incorporate the teachings of the Reborn into her faith, hoping that loyal servants and chosen lovers might in this way not be lost to time but rediscovered again and again with each rising. This has had occasional success, but it has also drawn the attention of unexpected enemies. There is, in particular, a sect of Tibetan Buddhists who became hunters of the unnatural long ago, believing that any entity that walks the Earth untouched by time (be it ghosts, vampires, immortals, and most especially Mummies) is an abomination that is not only removed from the sacred cycles but in fact delays and poisons the ability of other seekers of enlightenment from transcending the suffering of the world. She has clashed with them many times, and lost too many mortal allies to count to their damnable hunts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T18:23:21-07:00","id":1493375,"title":"","content":"I like it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-20T19:20:31-07:00","id":1493448,"title":"","content":"So I assume I should wait to hear a decision about space and such?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-21T15:47:20-07:00","id":1493486,"title":"","content":"Really great stuff ! My character is perhaps not as fully fleshed out yet, but some things I've determined.<br /> <br /> Mut-Em-Kheri-Min (&quot;Death Now In Front of My Face&quot;) bears a name assigned to them far into the cycle of their rebirths - a sentence from a poem from the kingdom of Khem, <i>The Dispute Between a Man and His Ba</i>. Those closest to them sometimes receive the right to qualify them by an older pronunciation of the quote's first word, Maawat. But this is not their name. Mut-Em-Kheri-Min has no name.<br /> <br /> The rough, irregular ring fastened around their neck during henet may inform a Deathless witness that Mut-Em-Kheri-Min once stood before the ore kilns of the House of Gold and Bronze. They failed, and thus fell into slavedom, a factotum to the Mesen-Nebu. Did their devotion to those Born of Gold earn the interest of another Guild then ? Or was such failure a mere ploy ? Regardless, it's through that recondite path that Maawat garnered the approval and initiation of the Maa-Kep, and delicate bone pendants and pearl ornaments now adorn the twisted ring of their failure.<br /> <br /> Mut-Em-Kheri-Min is, indeed, not their name. They had many, so many. Each ploy and stratagem added an alias, an epithet. And that dim clamor followed them, when time collapsed on itself, whispers like asps coiling around their soul. Their Ren was tattered from all this noise, but that made it all the more useful to pass the gates and trials of Duat.<br /> <br /> And that name was heard by Nefer-Tem, son of Sekhmet, Judge of the Never-Closing Blossom, whose scent rises to the nostrils of Ra as he sails the night sky, whose flower - the blue lotus of the Nile - addled the mind and entranced the senses of devotees and vagrants alike. He adjudicates fine and ambiguous distinctions, not least amongst which is mankind's entitlement (and enslavement) to its own dreams.<br /> <br /> Dreams, whether nightly visions, daydreams about one's hopes, drug-induced visions, echoes of the Astral realm, or all of the above, reflect the divine intent of the Shani'atu. Thus, the law of the Judges condemn both those who pursue a hopeless dream, and those who don't dare to pursue a sincere one. Therein lies the point that some emissaries of Nefer-Tem (Mut-Em-Kheri-Min among them) must adjudicate. Through Sorcery and Relics, access to the Astral might be secured - but the Arisen are clearly not the fittest creatures to roam the Invisible Realm...<br /> <br /> Maawat's cult did spread from the Near East to Europe to follow opium, and travelled the Silk Roads to grow bhang. Most of them are bygones, former somebodies consumed by the revelation they dreamed for something even bigger that what they received. Many of them become proficient drug-dealers and smugglers, and attach themselves to figures close enough to their ancient glory so they can vicariously live the dream of the life they could have been. The cult shows an intense respect for people lucidly embarking on bouts of self-destruction, and will use all of their resources to nurture and protect someone willing to live fast and die young.<br /> <br /> Mut-Em-Kheri-Min and their cult have a very external grasp on Kamakhya. They quickly took hold over the British exploitation of Assamese tea, and used this to probe the locals for rituals and lore for decades. They understand the trance and the tremors of the possessed: the struggles of power between the clergy and the folk ritualists. But they remain foreign, remote. They're trying to change that.<br /> <br /> Mut-Em-Kheri-Min has no name. Rumor goes, they once gave it away, when Irem still stood proud, to a handsome lissom dancer of the Akhem-Urtu - a scion of the Will, a student of the Word, a member of the Lost Guild whose restless stars have disappeared forever more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","user":"Adrasalieth","date":". 09-28-2022, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-21T16:06:20-07:00","id":1493487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Adrasalieth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1488093-recruiting-mummy-the-curse-2nd-edition?p=1493486#post1493486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really great stuff ! My character is perhaps not as fully fleshed out yet, but some things I've determined.<br /> <br /> Mut-Em-Kheri-Min (&quot;Death Now In Front of My Face&quot;) bears a name assigned to them far into the cycle of their rebirths - a sentence from a poem from the kingdom of Khem, <i>The Dispute Between a Man and His Ba</i>. Those closest to them sometimes receive the right to qualify them by an older pr