t":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1488093-recruiting-mummy-the-curse-2nd-edition?p=1493448#post1493448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I assume I should wait to hear a decision about space and such?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not needed. Welcome aboard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-21T17:24:30-07:00","id":1493493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1488093-recruiting-mummy-the-curse-2nd-edition?p=1493487#post1493487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> BACKGROUND <i>ABSOLUTELY</i> APPROVED. Bravo, sir.<br /> <br /> Will they have a Relic giving some degree of connection to the Astral Realms?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be the plan, yeah: either that or a fitting Rite. Clearly not Beast/Mage/Changeling level of ease within dreams, and hopefully something flavorful to Mummy. Like... hijacking your Cult's dreams, and acting in the Astral using their Reach/Grasp in some way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-21T18:11:37-07:00","id":1493495,"title":"","content":"The dreams of the dying/terminally ill? Goetia centered around the survival-instinct or symbolic representations of human mortality? (\u201c<b>I AM PALE CORPSE. I ROOT IN YOUR DREAMS, LITTLE MAN, AS YOUR BODY DEVOURS ITSELF WITH WILD ABANDON.</b>\u201d)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-26T11:09:19-07:00","id":1493747,"title":"","content":"Some more info:<br /> <br /> <b>Kamakhya\u2019s benbenet</b><br /> The \u2018child goddess\u2019 worshipped at Kamakhya in mortal form is usually just that: a little girl people believe has divinity. No magic surrounds her, no divinity dwells within her. This makes her eminently useful to the Arisen, who may work Utterances on her behalf while claiming <i>she</i> is the one doing so.<br /> <br /> Sometimes...sometimes the claim to divinity is <i>real</i>, as this child becomes a benebenet for a Judge. The earth cracks, locusts swarm, mundane rats build primitive shrines offering screeching nothings as devotion, cattle are born with heads split down the middle, tumors gain faces and utter prophecies: a Judge has manifested. The sky turns red and divine mandates are either broken or upheld.<br /> <br /> The Arisen of Kamakhya <i>fear</i> such an event. They live in dread of what a god of Duat might want in an area this removed from the Nameless Empire. And they fear for good reason: more Indian benbenets have been this priestess\u2019 position for many centuries. The child-goddesses seem to draw the Judges, though for what reason the Arisen may only guess fearfully and with great concern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 09-26-2022, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-26T16:46:42-07:00","id":1493783,"title":"","content":"Some more info:<br /> <br /> <b>Kamakhya\u2019s Astral reflection</b><br /> As one PC has a mild connection to the Astral Realms, I felt it best to describe a portion of cosmology not normally relevant to Mummy: The Curse.<br /> <br /> <i>The crown of fire sits in a place beyond the Arisen, and it burns with the waxing and waning of the sun. The crown is divinity, the idea a mortal can ascend through the proclamation of the believers. She who wears the crown is a goddess, and the dreams of gods bow down to her. Should she somehow commune with Goetia, these alien things will do as she says. As few child-goddesses can do this, this power is almost never used.<br /> <br /> Surrounding the burning crown are deep, still waters, wherein swim abyssal <i>things</i> that have long ago interbred with terrified human slaves. These fish-gods consider the crown theirs, and the child-goddess their representative.<br /> <br /> The crown sits upon a cushion in a ruined temple in the sky, and prayer-spirits in the shapes of mandalas tend to it. These manasaputra care only for the traditions of Kamakhya, and will tolerate only the right dogma. <br /> <br /> But when the benbenet rises, the clouds turn to storms and a vast shadow stretches across the sky. Instead of divine assurance, fear rises to strangle everything. The fish-demons swim deep in fear, abandoning their self-imposed posts. The crown gutters and burns low. The child-goddess wears a</i> different <i>crown, then, a black, charred ruin that was once magnificent.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 11-11-2022, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-27T12:12:18-07:00","id":1493844,"title":"","content":"Nothri:<br /> Do you have any ideas concerning these Tibetan Buddhist hunters that come to hunt immortals? Do they have Sekhem sorcerers, stolen Utterances castable with the aid of relics, things like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-27T15:11:22-07:00","id":1493863,"title":"","content":"The original concept for the group comes from an old game of mine in which they were a scorpion cult of a Shuankhsen who was trying to corrupt Buddhist doctrine for her own ends (long story short, many of their rites and meditations were originally blasphemous invocations to the Devourer, and their twisted road to 'Nirvana' and an end to suffering was a recipe for sending their souls plummeting straight into Ammit's jaws). But no, I did not have any particular details about their resources beyond my usual notes on the subject, e.g. 'they are as powerful as they need to be in order to be a threat at whatever Sekhem level the meret finds itself at the time'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-27T15:17:53-07:00","id":1493864,"title":"","content":"<b>Neter-Kherter and Kamakhya</b><br /> Neter-Khertet is not just in Egypt and North Africa; it covers the whole world, a place that is everywhere at once, a nonpoint in infinity. It covers Kamakhya as well, and it is no safer here than it is anywhere else, and indeed, has dangers unique to it.<br /> <br /> Fiends unique to India\u2019s Neter-Khertet may be found near Kamakhya, and take the forms of towering hags coated in gore, dragging huge iron pots behind them. They snatch up shades as they find and cook them in these pots, which they light with vomit made of boiling flesh and molten iron. These hags find mummies particularly appetizing, but hunger wracks them constantly, and the Law of Suffering says they can never be satiated.<br /> <br /> Kamakhya\u2019s shades appear daze and out of it, surprised and horrified by everything they find. Word of Shezmu quickly reaches them, and they learn the \u2018true\u2019 gods are nowhere near as benevolent as they\u2019d been led to believe. No reincarnation awaits them, only stomping feet and the cruel jaws of devouring gods.<br /> <br /> False Brahmins, fiends in disguise, wander to and fro, backwards-facing hands and feet and charcoal-black faces all that gives them away. They offer shades libations of blood; those foolish enough to drink from them are now cursed to remain aware even as Shezmu\u2019s feet crush them, only reaching quiet oblivion as the indolent gods of Duat drink their wine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-27T15:19:27-07:00","id":1493866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1488093-recruiting-mummy-the-curse-2nd-edition?p=1493863#post1493863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original concept for the group comes from an old game of mine in which they were a scorpion cult of a Shuankhsen who was trying to corrupt Buddhist doctrine for her own ends (long story short, many of their rites and meditations were originally blasphemous invocations to the Devourer, and their twisted road to 'Nirvana' and an end to suffering was a recipe for sending their souls plummeting straight into Ammit's jaws). But no, I did not have any particular details about their resources beyond my usual notes on the subject, e.g. 'they are as powerful as they need to be in order to be a threat at whatever Sekhem level the meret finds itself at the time'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, ok! I\u2019ll make stuff up, then... Are they still led by Shuankhsen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-28T08:46:07-07:00","id":1493903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1488093-recruiting-mummy-the-curse-2nd-edition?p=1493866#post1493866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, ok! I\u2019ll make stuff up, then... Are they still led by Shuankhsen?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At this point the Shuankhsen maintains a cult with a cult. The movement is large enough that it has expanded beyond her direct control, as was intended (souls delivered to the Devourer under her direct supervision is good, souls passively corrupted and sent her way as a result of adherence to your rituals and doctrines even while you sleep is better). Basically she has agents with the various sects and cults born from her original movement to act as eyes and ears and coax the movement in certain directions when necessary. She is of course aware that the very doctrine she instilled in them makes her as much a target as any mummy, so best to keep a low profile except among those loyal and aware of the cult's actual origin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-28T08:51:29-07:00","id":1493904,"title":"","content":"And if part of this is starting to sound a little familiar to you just know I wasn't consciously at the time setting out to emulate the relationship between Raziel and the Elder God from Legacy of Kain but I think some of the inspiration did leak into my head from that franchise anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-28T10:09:58-07:00","id":1493908,"title":"","content":"Ehhhh, ultimately every idea is influenced by an older idea. Don\u2019t sweat it!<br /> <br /> In Hunter: The Vigil terms, what would be their Endowment? Crazy cannibal Tibetan Buddhist monks screams \u2018f\u2019d up sorcery\u2019 of some kind. Or, if you\u2019d prefer, how could I replicate what they do solely using Mummy: The Curse 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-03T11:02:01-07:00","id":1494236,"title":"","content":"<b>The Black Bull</b><br /> Though only mummies have survived his appearances, as he will not attack them willingly, an...<i>entity</i>...called the Black Bull invisibly protects Kamakhya. Normally invisible and inaudible, yet not to be found in Neter-Khertet, the Black Bull manifests as an enormous obsidian-skinned, white-painted humanoid elephant. The Black Bull manifests whenever the temple itself is threatened by some overpoweringly strong occult menaces. His weaponry varies on what he is facing:<br /> <br /> Against vampires, he wields arms made of genuine sunlight.<br /> <br /> Against werewolves, he hefts a giant silver hammer.<br /> <br /> Against mages, he boasts a shield that shatters magic.<br /> <br /> And so on and so forth.<br /> <br /> He tries to talk to mummies, however, claiming some \u2018debt\u2019 owed to one of the Arisen in ages past. If the Arisen still won\u2019t listen to reason, even after several attempts, the Black Bull lifts an ivory horn to his lips and blows a powerful, disharmonic note...<i>and all the daitya gather as one</i>, to smite whomever the Black Bull decrees.<br /> <br /> The Black Bull doesn\u2019t talk about his past, his nature or even the debt he owes and to who he owes it. He doesn\u2019t talk about whatever realm he comes from. He refuses to use daitya against non-Arisen, nor will he talk about <i>how</i> it is the Black Bull <i>commands</i> the daitya.<br /> <br /> He is an enigma,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-03T12:26:58-07:00","id":1494249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1488093-recruiting-mummy-the-curse-2nd-edition?p=1493908#post1493908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ehhhh, ultimately every idea is influenced by an older idea. Don\u2019t sweat it!<br /> <br /> In Hunter: The Vigil terms, what would be their Endowment? Crazy cannibal Tibetan Buddhist monks screams \u2018f\u2019d up sorcery\u2019 of some kind. Or, if you\u2019d prefer, how could I replicate what they do solely using Mummy: The Curse 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Given there MO it could be some kind of banishing power, something that slowly drives vamps into torpor, ghosts into their anchors (or whatever the term is these days) and mummies into a death cycle. Perhaps some sustained chant that takes time to have an effect but can be performed at a distance? Sort of thing that creates a ticking clock for a super to hunt down and shut a clandestined temple down before the ritual fully takes effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-03T12:33:23-07:00","id":1494250,"title":"","content":"Hmmm....maybe it takes a certain length of time relevant to the Supernatural Tolerance trait of each supernatural being? Say each type of monster requires different elements be in the Rite? (Human blood for vampires, wolfsbane for werewolves, iron nails for fae, and so on)? Then, after the ritual, they have a set amount of time to hunt their target?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-09T14:47:29-07:00","id":1494700,"title":"","content":"Alright! Let\u2019s see some character writeups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-09T18:13:33-07:00","id":1494707,"title":"","content":"Have a funeral coming up this week so probably won't hear much from me until the 16th. Helping family get ready, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-09T18:20:23-07:00","id":1494708,"title":"","content":"Oh, wow. I am so sorry for your loss. Take whatever time you need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank"